IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`
IMPORT `g1-art2-governor-misconduct`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`

-- ind-a-tests-art2.l4: independent tests of Article 2 (entity, Jersey entity, constitution, constitutional Law, purpose, governor, relevant unincorporated entity, misconduct).
-- Expected values from WORK/ind-a/expectations.md (S2.x-nn). Assertions that disagree with the encoding live in ind-a-tests-disagree.l4 or ind-a-tests-ambiguous.l4.

§ `ind-a tests: Article 2`

§§ `Helpers`

`ind-a I` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
`ind-a today` MEANS `the text of 2 October 2026`

GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`ind-a kinds today` facts MEANS `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `ind-a I` `ind-a today` facts

GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a Jersey entity today` facts MEANS `Art 2(3) the body is a Jersey entity` `ind-a I` `ind-a today` facts

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`ind-a kinds on` d facts MEANS `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `ind-a I` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` d `the favoured interpretation`) facts

§§ `2(1) entity (S2.1-01 to S2.1-19)`

-- S2.1-01 (a) trustees of a trust (src:49)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a trustees of a Jersey trust` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`
-- S2.1-02 (b) fidéicommissaires (src:50)
#ASSERT elem `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a fideicommissaires`)
-- S2.1-03 (ba) on 2025-10-16 (src:51-54; R&O.56/2025)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds on` (YMD 2025 10 16) `ind-a Jersey NPO body corporate` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
-- S2.1-04 the same body on 2025-10-15 -> not an entity
#ASSERT null (`ind-a kinds on` (YMD 2025 10 15) `ind-a Jersey NPO body corporate`)
-- S2.1-05 a non-NPO Jersey body corporate within none of (c) to (h) -> not an entity
#ASSERT null (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey non-NPO body corporate`)
-- S2.1-06 a Guernsey NPO body corporate (fails (ba)(ii)); with no similarity stated, not (j) either
#ASSERT NOT elem `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Guernsey NPO body corporate`)
-- S2.1-06 with AMBIG-1: the same Guernsey body judged substantially similar to a (ba) body is within (j) on my reading ((ba) inside "(a) to (h)"), and not on the other
#ASSERT elem `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction` (`ind-a kinds today` (`ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a NPO`, `ind-a established under foreign law`) (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY))
#ASSERT null (`Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.1 read the other way` `ind-a today` (`ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a NPO`, `ind-a established under foreign law`) (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY))
-- S2.1-07 an NPO that is a Jersey company -> (f), not (ba)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey company that is an NPO` EQUALS LIST `a company`
-- S2.1-08 incorporated 1862 association -> (c)
#ASSERT elem `an incorporated 1862 association` (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a 1862 association`)
-- S2.1-09 foundation -> (d)
#ASSERT elem `a foundation` (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey foundation body`)
-- S2.1-10 (e): by an enactment, by Act of the States, by Royal Charter in relation to Jersey
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a body established by a Law` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a body established by Act of the States` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a body established by Royal Charter for Jersey` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
-- S2.1-11 Jersey company -> (f)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey company body` EQUALS LIST `a company`
-- S2.1-12 LLC under another Jersey enactment -> (g)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey LLC` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
-- S2.1-13 body under a UK Act extended to Jersey -> (h)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a body under a UK Act` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`
-- S2.1-14 unincorporated association -> (i)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey association with a resident governor` EQUALS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
-- S2.1-15 partnership -> not an entity
#ASSERT null (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a partnership body`)
-- S2.1-16 English charitable company similar to a Jersey company -> (j)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a English charitable company` EQUALS LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
-- S2.1-17 French unincorporated association -> (i), not (j)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a French association` EQUALS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
-- S2.1-18 Jersey company as sole trustee -> (a) and (f)
#ASSERT `ind-a kinds today` `ind-a Jersey company as sole trustee` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`
-- S2.1-19 a lone individual -> not an entity
#ASSERT null (`ind-a kinds today` `ind-a lone individual`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1) the body is an entity` `ind-a I` `ind-a today` `ind-a lone individual`

§§ `2(2) the Minister's power (S2.2-01 to S2.2-03)`

-- S2.2-01 R&O.56/2025 was made on 2025-10-09 by the Minister for External Relations, who was "the Minister" that day
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` (YMD 2025 10 9) `the favoured interpretation`) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S2.2-02 the Chief Minister was not "the Minister" on 2025-10-09
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` (YMD 2025 10 9) `the favoured interpretation`) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`)
-- S2.2-03 the power is to add only: the only act under Article 2 is to add a sub-paragraph (a MAY of the Minister)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 2(2) the Minister may add a sub-paragraph to Article 2(1)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`make an Order adding a sub-paragraph to Article 2(1)` "(ba)") AT 1

§§ `2(3) Jersey entity (S2.3-01 to S2.3-18)`

-- S2.3-01..08 each of (a) to (h) -> Jersey entity
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a trustees of a Jersey trust`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a fideicommissaires`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a 1862 association`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey foundation body`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a body established by Act of the States`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey company body`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey LLC`
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a body under a UK Act`
-- S2.3-09 a (ba) body: my reading, inside "(a) to (h)" -> TRUE
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey NPO body corporate`
-- S2.3-10 (j) only -> FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a English charitable company`
-- S2.3-11 (i), Jersey law, a governor resident in Jersey -> TRUE
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey association with a resident governor`
-- S2.3-12 (i), Jersey law, a Jersey company governor -> TRUE
#ASSERT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey association with a company governor`
-- S2.3-13 (i), Jersey law, governor a Jersey entity only by 2(3)(b) -> FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey association with an association governor`
-- S2.3-14 (i), English law, resident governor -> FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a English-law association with a resident governor`
-- S2.3-15 (i), Jersey law, governors resident in Guernsey -> FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey association with Guernsey governors`
-- S2.3-16 (i), Jersey law, an English company governor -> FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Jersey entity today` `ind-a Jersey association with an English company governor`
-- S2.3-09 on the other reading of the range: FALSE (both readings are written in expectations; this pins the other reading's function)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(3) the body is a Jersey entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.1 read the other way` `ind-a today` `ind-a Jersey NPO body corporate`

§§ `2(4) constitution (S2.4-01 to S2.4-08)`

#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `the trustees of a trust` EQUALS "the terms of the trust"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `a foundation` EQUALS "the charter and regulations of the foundation"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `a company` EQUALS "the memorandum and articles of association of the company"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` EQUALS "the enactment, Act of the States or Royal Charter that established the body corporate"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `an unincorporated body or association of persons` EQUALS "any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` EQUALS "any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction` EQUALS "any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` EQUALS "any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `an incorporated 1862 association` EQUALS "the Act of the court incorporating it under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862, and the object and rules approved or modified under that Article"
-- S2.4-02 a court-approved fidéicommis (src:74)
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` EQUALS "the minute of the contract annexed to the application to the court for the creation of the fidéicommis, any other documents so annexed, and any authorisation granted by the court under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862 in respect of the fidéicommis"
-- S2.4-08 company as sole trustee: AMBIG-3; the first reading (every case) gives both, the second gives the trust's terms only
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity in all its kinds consists of` `ind-a I` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) EQUALS LIST "the terms of the trust", "the memorandum and articles of association of the company"
#ASSERT `Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity in all its kinds consists of` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) EQUALS LIST "the terms of the trust"

§§ `2(5) constitutional Law (S2.5-01 to S2.5-08)`

#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `the trustees of a trust` `ind-a trustees of a Jersey trust` EQUALS JUST `the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984`
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` `ind-a fideicommissaires` EQUALS JUST `the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `an incorporated 1862 association` `ind-a 1862 association` EQUALS JUST `the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a foundation` `ind-a Jersey foundation body` EQUALS JUST `the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009`
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a company` `ind-a Jersey company body` EQUALS JUST `the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
-- S2.5-05 a body incorporated BY a Law -> that Law
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` `ind-a body established by a Law` EQUALS JUST (`another Law by which the body corporate was incorporated` "Jersey Heritage (Jersey) Law 2099")
-- S2.5-06 Act of the States; Royal Charter -> none
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` `ind-a body established by Act of the States` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` `ind-a body established by Royal Charter for Jersey` EQUALS NOTHING
-- S2.5-07 a (g) LLC: AMBIG-2, my reading literal -> none; the other reading -> the LLC Law
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` `ind-a Jersey LLC` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.3 read the other way` `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` `ind-a Jersey LLC` EQUALS JUST (`the enactment under which the body was incorporated` "Limited Liability Companies (Jersey) Law 2018")
-- S2.5-08 (h), (i), (j), (ba) -> none
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` `ind-a body under a UK Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `an unincorporated body or association of persons` `ind-a Jersey association with a resident governor` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction` `ind-a English charitable company` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `ind-a I` `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` `ind-a Jersey NPO body corporate` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `2(6) purpose (S2.6-01 to S2.6-04)`

#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `the trustees of a trust` EQUALS "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` EQUALS "the objects for which it was created or incorporated, or that were subsequently authorized under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `an incorporated 1862 association` EQUALS "the objects for which it was created or incorporated, or that were subsequently authorized under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `a foundation` EQUALS "the objects specified in its charter or its regulations"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `a company` EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `an unincorporated body or association of persons` EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"

§§ `2(7) to 2(9) governor (S2.7-01 to S2.8-05)`

GIVEN tr IS A BOOLEAN, cm IS A BOOLEAN, dr IS A BOOLEAN, mc IS A BOOLEAN, rel IS A `Relation to the general control and management`
GIVETH A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
`ind-a role` tr cm dr mc rel MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS tr
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS cm
        `a director of the company` IS dr
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS mc
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS rel

`ind-a no role` MEANS `ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`

GIVEN conforms IS A BOOLEAN, byCommissioner IS A BOOLEAN, committee IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
`ind-a model` conforms byCommissioner committee MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS conforms
        `published by the Commissioner` IS
            `Facts about a publication` WITH
                `made available by the person in some manner` IS byCommissioner
                `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS byCommissioner
                `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS byCommissioner
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS byCommissioner
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS committee

`ind-a no model` MEANS `ind-a model` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind-a the Commissioner's model with a committee` MEANS `ind-a model` TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      md IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
      rl IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a governor of` ks md rl MEANS `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `ind-a I` ks md rl

-- S2.7-01 trustee -> governor; fidéicommissaire -> governor (src:92)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
-- S2.7-02 council member -> governor; a guardian who is not a council member -> not (src:93)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `a foundation`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `a foundation`) `ind-a no model` `ind-a no role`
-- S2.7-03 director -> governor; secretary or shareholder (no role) -> not (src:94)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `a company`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `a company`) `ind-a no model` `ind-a no role`
-- S2.7-04 relevant unincorporated entity: committee member -> governor; ordinary member -> not (src:95)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `ind-a the Commissioner's model with a committee` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `holds none of the general control and management`)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `ind-a the Commissioner's model with a committee` `ind-a no role`
-- S2.7-05 any other case: general control and management under the constitution -> governor (src:96)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds the general control and management alone`)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds the general control and management alone`)
-- S2.7-06 2(9)(a): an employee exercising control for those who have it in their own right -> not a governor (src:103)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`)
-- S2.7-07 2(9)(b): alone or as one of a number -> governor (src:104)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`)
-- S2.7-08 company as sole trustee (AMBIG-3): every case -> the company (as trustee) and a director are governors; first case only -> the director is not
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
#ASSERT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) `ind-a no model` (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `holds none of the general control and management`)
-- S2.8-01 conforms to the Commissioner's published model with a committee -> relevant (src:97-101)
#ASSERT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `ind-a I` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `ind-a the Commissioner's model with a committee`
-- S2.8-02 bespoke constitution (does not conform) -> not relevant; its committee member is a governor only through 2(7)(e)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `ind-a I` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) (`ind-a model` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a governor of` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) (`ind-a model` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`ind-a role` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `holds none of the general control and management`)
-- S2.8-03 conforms to a Commissioner model without a committee -> not relevant
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `ind-a I` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) (`ind-a model` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S2.8-04 a company using the model -> not relevant
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `ind-a I` (LIST `a company`) `ind-a the Commissioner's model with a committee`
-- S2.8-05 model published by a third party -> not relevant
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `ind-a I` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) (`ind-a model` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `2(10) misconduct (S2.10-01 to S2.10-16)`

GIVEN atConduct IS A `Standing on the register`
      byCharityOrGovernor IS A BOOLEAN
      breachConstitution IS A BOOLEAN
      breachConstLaw IS A BOOLEAN
      breachRSN IS A BOOLEAN
      breachCourtOrderThisLaw IS A BOOLEAN
      inRelation IS A BOOLEAN
      equivalentForeign IS A BOOLEAN
      offConstLaw IS A BOOLEAN
      offFS IS A BOOLEAN
      offTax IS A BOOLEAN
      offML IS A BOOLEAN
      offDishonesty IS A BOOLEAN
      offForeign IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
`ind-a conduct` atConduct byCharityOrGovernor breachConstitution breachConstLaw breachRSN breachCourtOrderThisLaw inRelation equivalentForeign offConstLaw offFS offTax offML offDishonesty offForeign MEANS
    `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` WITH
        `standing of the entity when the conduct occurred` IS atConduct
        `standing of the entity when the question is asked` IS atConduct
        `the constitutional Laws of the charity` IS LIST `the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
        `an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS equivalentForeign
        `by the registered charity or by one of its governors` IS byCharityOrGovernor
        `a contravention of a provision of the constitution of the registered charity` IS breachConstitution
        `a contravention of a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity` IS breachConstLaw
        `a contravention of a provision of a required steps notice` IS breachRSN
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under this Law` IS breachCourtOrderThisLaw
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE
        `the offence is in relation to the entity` IS inRelation
        `an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity` IS offConstLaw
        `an offence under the financial services Laws, any Regulation or Order made under them, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012` IS offFS
        `an offence under the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961, the Goods and Services Tax (Jersey) Law 2007 or the Taxation (Land Transactions) (Jersey) Law 2009` IS offTax
        `an offence under any other enactment relating to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS offML
        `an offence under any other enactment or under customary law involving deception or dishonesty` IS offDishonesty
        `an offence under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey similar to one listed in (i) to (v)` IS offForeign

`ind-a an RSN on the charity` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 3 1
        `steps to be taken by` IS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS FALSE

GIVEN c IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
      efc IS A BOOLEAN
      thisLaw IS A BOOLEAN
      rsns IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a misconduct` c efc thisLaw rsns MEANS `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `ind-a I` c efc thisLaw rsns

`ind-a g` MEANS `entered in the general section`

-- S2.10-01 a registered charity contravenes a provision of this Law (12(7)) -> misconduct (src:106-107)
#ASSERT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `ind-a g` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
-- S2.10-03 the charity contravenes its constitution; a governor contravenes the constitutional Law -> misconduct (src:108)
#ASSERT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `ind-a g` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE EMPTY
#ASSERT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `ind-a g` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE EMPTY
-- S2.10-04 contravention of a required steps notice -> misconduct (src:109)
#ASSERT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `ind-a g` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE (LIST `ind-a an RSN on the charity`)
-- S2.10-05 contravention of a court order under this Law -> misconduct (src:110)
#ASSERT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `ind-a g` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE EMPTY
-- S2.10-06 a non-governor employee contravenes the constitution -> not (a) misconduct (src:106)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `ind-a g` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE EMPTY
-- S2.10-07 an applicant not yet registered contravenes this Law -> not (a) misconduct (src:106)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a misconduct` (`ind-a conduct` `an applicant for registration` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
